From 7261922855d85278b7f8931adb7be08b9d8ddd33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:34:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] fs: r9fs: make RPC waits killable and wake waiters on
 device removal

A stalled 9P server or a removed device left callers of r9fs in
uninterruptible sleep, holding the channel mutex, and blocked driver
removal behind them.

- rust: sync: add Completion::wait_for_completion_killable() and
  Mutex::lock_killable() (with a mutex_lock_killable helper).
- Wait for replies killably. A killed waiter leaves its request posted
  (buffers stay with the device) and marks it pending; the next user
  of the channel reaps the stale reply before posting its own request.
- Device removal sets a removed flag and calls complete_all() before
  taking the channel mutex, so a waiter fails with EIO instead of
  waiting for a reply a removed device may never deliver.
- Clunks never wait: one that finds the channel busy or pending is
  queued and sent before the next request (dropped on Tversion), so a
  killed task's file release does not block on the abandoned reply.
